tatus="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8139351</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8254813-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8254813</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1045454A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>CITIZEN WATCH CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYOSHI KOZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CITIZEN WATCH CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYOSHI, KOZO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYOSHI KOZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYOSHI, KOZO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A high-quality solar cell the interface of which is free from contamination is disclosed. On a substrate, a transparent electrode film, an amorphous silicon film, and a metal electrode film are successively formed in multilayer and etched to a desired pattern by using a resist film having two thicknesses. Solar cell elements are insulated from each other through a predetermined protective film, and a conductive paste is applied over the protective film to electrically connect the solar cell elements in series.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une cellule solaire de qualité élevée dont l'interface est exempte de contamination. Un film d'électrode transparent, un film de silicium amorphe, et un film d'électrode métallique sont successivement formés en plusieurs couches sur un substrat, et gravés selon un motif désiré au moyen d'un film de résist à deux épaisseurs. Les éléments de cellule solaire sont isolés les uns des autres par l'intermédiaire d'un film de protection, et une pâte conductrice est appliquée sur le film de protection afin de monter électriquement en série, les éléments de cellule solaire.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>